From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:15:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/44] qwen27: initialise the vision dump before it is read

A created struct carries no field defaults, so Tower.dump was undefined rather
than the empty slice it declares, and a run with TF_QWEN_VISION_BLOCKS unset read
through a garbage pointer in the test host. Fixed by setting it at load, which is
what keeps an unset run free.

Found because a served image request segfaulted in the tower's encode; the dump
is now off by default and costs one comparison a block.
---
 zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig b/zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig
index 13d9944b9..7f10dc357 100644
--- a/zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig
+++ b/zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig
@@ -142,6 +142,8 @@ pub const Tower = struct {
         errdefer gpa.destroy(t);
         t.gpa = gpa;
         t.device = device;
+        // a created struct carries no field defaults: every field is set here or below
+        t.dump = &.{};
         t.c = c;
         t.k = try Kernels.load(gpa, device);
         errdefer t.k.deinit();
